{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 19, :comments ["<b>The first of the first-fruits, etc.</b> Perhaps it alludes that one should not waste his seed, and that the first drop that issues from him should be brought to the House of YHWH, in the manner of their saying (Yoma 2a) 'his house' — this is his wife." "And it is precise to say <b>the House of YHWH</b> to exclude the house of a zonah, and this is a commandment that our father Jacob, peace be upon him, fulfilled, as it is written (Genesis 49:3): ״כֹּחִי וְרֵאשִׁית אוֹנִי״." "And it concluded by saying <b>you shall not cook a kid in its mother's milk</b> to allude a great sod: for those who waste their seed cause the death of little ones from between their mother's breasts, as it explained the matter in its saying in the verse (Micah 6:7): ״הַאֶתֵּן בְּכוֹרִי פִּשְׁעִי פְּרִי בִטְנִי חַטַּאת נַפְשִׁי״ — for when a man wastes his seed, an evil destroying force is created from it, and it subsequently gains dominion over the son who is born; and these are the oppressed souls spoken of in the holy Zohar (vol. I, 219a); and who caused this? That he did not bring his first-fruits to the House of YHWH." "And according to the plain sense, the reason it juxtaposed <b>you shall not cook</b>, etc., with the first-fruits is to say (Hullin 114b) that meat in milk is forbidden for benefit — which is the core of the halakhah. It intended to juxtapose it with the first-fruits to indicate that they too are forbidden for benefit (Rambam, Laws of Bikkurim, chapter 2); and see in the book Pri To'ar."], :book :exodus, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 23, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T19:33:00.875155706Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}